        "original_id": "85d71f61-42b7-53cb-93ef-3c577ec79d43",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Halldór Laxness, Timothy Leary, Guðný Halldórsdóttir, Auður Laxness\n- Roles: writer, psychologist, textile designer, Nobel Prize winner\n- Topics: Icelandic literature, psychedelic drugs\n\nFacts:\n- Halldór Laxness was born as Halldór Guðjónsson on 23 April 1902 and became a twentieth-century Icelandic writer.\n- Timothy Leary was born on October 22, 1920 and became an American psychologist and writer.\n- Halldór Laxness won the Nobel Prize in 1955.\n- Timothy Leary was known for advocating the exploration of the therapeutic potential of psychedelic drugs under controlled conditions.\n- Timothy Leary died on May 31, 1996.\n- Halldór Laxness died on 8 February 1998.\n- Guðný Halldórsdóttir is the daughter of writer and 1955 Nobel Prize winner Halldór Laxness and writer and textile designer Auður Laxness.",
